    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (2/2 tests pass, `BUILD SUCCESS`). The only test classes in the project are `AcceptanceTest` (concrete) built on the abstract `AcceptanceBase`, and both its cases now pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an owner `registrationDate` that defaults to the server's current date when omitted and is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it flows into both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and response DTO (`OwnerDto`). `format: date` maps to `java.time.LocalDate` and serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`, matching the existing Pet `birthDate` handling.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the payload doesn't supply one; a supplied value is preserved (MapStruct maps it by name).\n- **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. The test profile is `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change was required for persistence.\n\nHow it satisfies the spec:\n- `coreDefaultsToToday` \u2014 no date supplied \u2192 server sets today \u2192 returned as today's ISO date. \u2713\n- `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` \u2014 `2020-06-15` supplied \u2192 preserved and returned. \u2713",
